rows=[(506, 'the-water-waits', 'The water waits', 'The poem ends with the crane not returning. An empty winter wetland honours that unresolved absence without fabricating a sighting of the named bird or pretending to document a particular Iranian location.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 wide and low quiet wetland in cool charcoal and dilute grey-blue watercolor. Almost flat shallow winter water extends across the frame, a low distant reed bed drawn in sparse uneven dark marks at the horizon. At left foreground a few dry reed stems lean from the cropped bank, partly overlapping one another; right two thirds mostly open calm water with subtle broken reflections, cloudy pale sky just above. No crane or other bird anywhere, no flight silhouette, no feathers, no footprints, no ghost shape. A habitable ordinary place with a felt absence, not a desolate apocalypse or scenic tourist wetland. Muted cool light, no bright sunset, fog spotlight, mountains, buildings, landmarks, text or people. Reeds rooted in bank, reflections subdued rather than mirrored perfectly.'), (510, 'red-earth-open-sky', 'Red earth, open sky', 'The speaker longs for release from institutional distance into red soil, green valleys and trees. A low earth-level view gives the ground dignity and lets a tree branch into open sky without illustrating a transformed human body.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 expressive matte gouache landscape with earthy red, muted olive and pale cream-blue. A low uneven bank of red lateritic soil crosses the lower third; one ordinary tree grows from its left side, trunk rising partly outside the top left and a few unequal branches reaching into the middle sky. Roots disappear firmly into the bank, not a decorative exposed root web. Beyond at right a soft unlabelled green valley recedes at ordinary scale. Viewpoint near soil level, broad hand-painted colour planes, sparse charcoal structure, soil clods close to foreground only. No mountains made into faces, body, skin, university, chains, magical glow, temple, roads or identifiable geographical claim. Pale open sky and calm daylight, not a heroic inspirational sunset. The red earth is matter with weight, not a luxurious fabric or polished desert.'), (513, 'a-quiet-lunar-companion', 'A quiet lunar companion', 'The moon keeps an intimate vigil over unuttered thoughts. A small ordinary moon above an understated roof edge offers companionship without literal flowers, bunny ears, tears or a gigantic fantasy moon.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 sparse soft pastel and matte indigo gouache nocturne. Deep but readable muted blue-violet sky occupies almost the entire frame; a small pale waxing gibbous moon above and right of centre, no larger than a thumbnail in the image, its light softly uneven with only the faintest grey suggestion of lunar surface. At the very bottom left a cropped plain roof edge and one short unadorned parapet make an ordinary place from which to look up; dark planes no elaborate architecture. A narrow thin cloud veil below the moon, not covering it, no dramatic nebula or star field. Quiet atmospheric falloff, moon is not a luminous lightbulb and casts no enormous spotlight. No face, rabbit, flowers, teardrops, giant craters, person at window, readable text, giant celestial body or reflected second moon. A restrained intimate night painting with selective soft edges, companionship without spectacle.')]
items=[]
for pid,ident,title,reason,scene in rows:
 p=S/f'content/editions/issue-27/poem-{pid}.json';d=json.loads(p.read_text());snapshot=B/f'poem-{pid}.json';snapshot.write_bytes(p.read_bytes())
 prompt=f'Use case: illustration-story. Original horizontal 3:2 literary artwork for Kabita Live Issue27. Human Natural in Poetic Natural mode. Preserve the selected expressive medium; a painted interpretation, never documentary evidence.\nEmotional anchor: {reason}\nScene and medium: {scene}\nAnti-optimization checks: avoid staged object display, equal detail everywhere, mechanically repeated shapes, theatrical lighting and cosmetic distress. Material contact, geometry and illumination must make sense. Preserve quiet negative space and emotional ambiguity. No identifiable real people, portraits, readable text, signature, logos or watermark. No people, portraits or documentary location claims. Opaque ivory-paper background.\nPoem {d["title"]} by {d["author"]}; source read fully, use as context only, never render the words:\n{d["text"]}\n'
